# Debugging: Memory Leak in WebSocket Handler

Spent 3 hours tracking down a memory leak in production.

## Symptoms
- RSS growing ~50MB/hour
- Eventually OOM killed after 18-24 hours
- Only on servers with >100 concurrent WS connections

## Root Cause
Event listeners were not being cleaned up on disconnect. Each connection registered a callback on the global event bus but the `on_disconnect` handler had a race condition -- if the client disconnected during a message send, the cleanup was skipped.

## Fix
```javascript
class ConnectionManager {
  disconnect(clientId) {
    // Always cleanup, regardless of state
    this.eventBus.removeAllListeners(clientId);
    this.connections.delete(clientId);
    this.metrics.decrement('active_connections');
  }
}
```

Memory now stable at ~200MB under same load.

# Error Handling Patterns in Async Python

Documenting our error handling conventions for the team.

## Rules
1. Never catch bare `Exception` -- always specific types
2. Use custom exception hierarchy
3. Log at the boundary, not in library code
4. Return structured errors from API

## Exception Hierarchy
```python
class AppError(Exception):
    status_code = 500

class NotFoundError(AppError):
    status_code = 404

class ValidationError(AppError):
    status_code = 422

class AuthError(AppError):
    status_code = 401
```

## API Error Response
```json
{
  "error": {
    "code": "VALIDATION_ERROR",
    "message": "Email is required",
    "details": {"field": "email"}
  }
}
```

# Nginx Reverse Proxy Configuration

Configured Nginx as reverse proxy for all services.

## Features
- SSL termination with Let's Encrypt
- HTTP/2 support
- Gzip compression
- Rate limiting per IP
- WebSocket upgrade support

```nginx
upstream api {
    server 127.0.0.1:8000;
    keepalive 32;
}

server {
    listen 443 ssl http2;
    server_name api.example.com;

    ssl_certificate /etc/letsencrypt/live/api.example.com/fullchain.pem;
    ssl_certificate_key /etc/letsencrypt/live/api.example.com/privkey.pem;

    location / {
        proxy_pass http://api;
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
    }

    location /ws {
        proxy_pass http://api;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;
        proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
        proxy_set_header Connection "upgrade";
    }
}
```

# Implementing Streaming LLM Responses

Added streaming support for LLM responses in our chat interface.

## Server-Side (FastAPI + SSE)
```python
@app.post('/api/chat/stream')
async def chat_stream(request: ChatRequest):
    async def generate():
        async for chunk in llm.stream(request.messages):
            yield f'data: {json.dumps({"text": chunk})}\n\n'
        yield 'data: [DONE]\n\n'
    return StreamingResponse(generate(), media_type='text/event-stream')
```

## Client-Side (JavaScript)
```javascript
const response = await fetch('/api/chat/stream', {
  method: 'POST',
  body: JSON.stringify({ messages }),
});
const reader = response.body.getReader();
const decoder = new TextDecoder();

while (true) {
  const { done, value } = await reader.read();
  if (done) break;
  const text = decoder.decode(value);
  appendToChat(text);
}
```

Time to first token: ~200ms. Users perceive much faster responses.

# TIL: CSS Container Queries

Finally, responsive design based on container, not viewport!

## The Problem
- Media queries based on viewport width
- Component doesn't know its container size
- Same component in sidebar vs main area = different viewport, same problem

## Container Queries Solution
```css
/* 1. Define containment context */
.card-container {
  container-type: inline-size;
  container-name: card;
}

/* 2. Query against container */
@container card (min-width: 400px) {
  .card {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 2fr;
  }
}

@container card (max-width: 399px) {
  .card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }
}
```

## Browser Support
- Chrome 105+
- Firefox 110+
- Safari 16+
- ~92% global coverage

This changes everything for component libraries. Components can now be truly self-contained and responsive.
